A||||3||86SE||1986 Fiero SE vs. 1993 Ford Tauras SHO||||5||
Z||000000||86SE||12-07-2000||11:40 PM||||A new guy in town just bought a 1993 Ford Tauras 24valve SHO 5 speed.  He dosent shift the greatest, and I think the ol Fiero can take it.  What do you think: Stock v6 Fiero with an auto vs a stock SHO Tauras with a 5 speed?<P>Place your bets, post the numbers....please.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://fierodude.hypermart.net/mysig.jpg"> <BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero -- 3.4L Conversion *SUSPENDED* --<BR>Special Rally Heavy Duty Suspention||||reg||5
Z||000001||Shiner||12-07-2000||11:57 PM||||Sorry, but that SHO should learn you some manners.  Before I bought the GT, I was seriously thinking about an SHO.  They are quick damn cars with the 5 speed.  As long as he doesn't launch it way too hard (front driver), he should beat you.  No offense meant to any of the auto Fiero guys here, but the V6 autos are slow compared to the M4 or M5 cars.  And I think with the same driver, a V6 stick Fiero should be pretty close competition for an SHO 5 speed.||||reg||1
Z||000002||86SE||12-08-2000||12:21 AM||||So you suggest I should beat him with NOS?<P>But just to give you an idea of his shifting capabilities, I was in my frinds Jeep Cherrokee and we actually raced him and we beat him off the gun, it took him a while to get it in second gear, but when he did he passed us and only pulled about 3 car legnths on us.  So the reason I say I can beat him is because when I raced his jeep with the Fiero I pulled about 4 car legnths on him right away, his front bumper never passed my front bumper.<P>We will see come spring.....unles he gets better at shifting..<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://fierodude.hypermart.net/mysig.jpg"> <BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero -- 3.4L Conversion *SUSPENDED* --<BR>Special Rally Heavy Duty Suspention||||reg||6
Z||000003||sqoach||12-08-2000||02:02 AM||||i agree with shiner on this one. a sho 5spd is damn quick. i drove my brother's before and that thing can haul. i was messin around with him in my fiero (86 4cyl 5spd) at a stoplight once. he's not as good as me at a manual tranny, so i kinda stayed with him at first, but he kicked my ass anyway. i wouldn't mess with those sho's, especially with an auto. i don't know the mods on your car so i wouldn't know for sure.<BR>just my 2 1/2 cents.<P>------------------<BR>sQoaCh<BR>fiero7@hotmail.com<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mysig_2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
